## Benchmarks — fetched, not included; what derives from them, included

    bench/bird/          BIRD mini-dev          CC BY-SA 4.0   (fetched by bench/fetch.sh)
    bench/livesql/data/  LiveSQLBench Large-v1  CC BY-SA 4.0   (fetched by bench/livesql/fetch.sh;
                                                               the gold is requested, never committed)
    bench/spider2/       Spider 2.0             MIT            (cloned by hand; see
                                                               bench/spider2-trial/README.md)

    BIRD          https://bird-bench.github.io/
    LiveSQLBench  https://huggingface.co/datasets/birdsql/livesqlbench-large-v1
                  (its dataset card states CC BY-SA 4.0; its metadata, CC BY 4.0)
    Spider 2.0    https://github.com/xlang-ai/Spider2

No benchmark's questions, evidence, databases, gold SQL or answer keys are
included, and nor are the files the runs copied them into: the pilot's sample
of BIRD (`bench/pilot/questions.json`, rebuilt by `bench/pilot/sample.py`), the
evidence each modeller was given (`bench/pilot/work/semantic/*/definitions.json`,
rebuilt by `bench/pilot/semantic/definitions.py`), the DDL, schema listings and
FORML of BIRD's databases (`bench/pilot/material/<db>.*`, rebuilt by
`bench/pilot/material.py` and `bench/ablation/models.py`), the Spider trial's
working copies (rebuilt by `bench/spider2-trial/build.py`), and the
seventy-question hand run (`bench/archive/hand-run/california.json`,
`toxicology.json` and their results).

Included, and derived from the benchmarks under their terms above:

  - Conceptual models of BIRD's databases, which restate their schemas — tables,
    columns, types and keys — in this project's model format
    (`bench/pilot/work/semantic/*/*.ccm.json`), with the definitions modeller
    agents wrote for them (`semantic.json`).
  - LiveSQLBench's declared foreign keys, as the answer key the reference
    inference is scored against, and a few sample values per column from BIRD
    and LiveSQLBench databases, as shown to a language model
    (`bench/ablation/work/`).
  - Short quotations of questions, evidence and knowledge-base entries in the
    write-ups, each identified by benchmark and question.

And this project's own record of what it did with them: the queries each
writer produced (`bench/*/work/*/*/answers*.json`), every query tried
(`attempts.jsonl`), and the scored results (`bench/pilot/results.json`,
`results-history/`, `bench/ablation/work/`). For LiveSQLBench, whose gold is
not public, the write-ups describe where an answer and the gold differed
without reproducing the gold.


